      "title": "Actual PBPS squared defect: positive complex lift",
      "source": {
        "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A2",
        "edition": "arXiv:2609.06905v1; Lean4.33.0/fixedMathlib",
        "anchor": "Appendix D.1 real Hilbert conventions and positive square-root background; B.10-B.11 actual all-macro square-root prerequisite, attributed ASTIS complexification completion, not a printed paper theorem.",
        "wording_status": "faithful paraphrase",
        "attribution": "Attributed ASTIS background completion supporting Fan Chen, Sinho Chewi, Jianfeng Lu and Matthew S. Zhang real positive-root prerequisite. This exact complexification is ASTIS-authored and is not a printed Γ/main theorem."
      },
      "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including the explicit rank-zero extension. Let V:E→ℝ be C², let 0<α≤β, and assume α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v. Assume η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, J as the law of (X,X+√η Z) for independent X∼μ,Z∼N(0,I), ν=J.snd, and Λ as the law of (Y,2X−Y) under J. The laws μ,J,ν are probabilities. There exists a Markov kernel S with, for every y, S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)), Λ.IsCondKernel S, Λ.fst=ν and Λ.snd=ν. There exists a selfadjoint bounded T on L²(ν;ℝ) such that for every u, ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx) ν-almost everywhere, and ∫Tu dν=∫u dν. Set D=I−T²; this exact full-domain squared defect is positive. Define the actual quotient maps ιu=u+0i, Rg=Re g, Qg=Im g and Cg=conj(g). Then ι preserves norm, Cg=g iff g=ιu for some real u, and there exists a bounded complex-linear positive Dc on L²(ν;ℂ) such that Dc g=ιD(Rg)+iιD(Qg), Dc(ιu)=ι(Du), and C(Dc g)=Dc(Cg), universally on their displayed domains. The operator T, positivity, kernel/law certificates and Dc are produced conclusions. No real Γ/root/descent/inverse is asserted.",
      "assumptions": [
        "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including the explicit rank-zero extension. Let V:E→ℝ be C², let 0<α≤β, and assume α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v. Assume η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, J as the law of (X,X+√η Z) for independent X∼μ,Z∼N(0,I), ν=J.snd, and Λ as the law of (Y,2X−Y) under J.",
        "All kernel, probability, T and D certificates are conclusions. Finite E does not imply finite L2; rank-zero E and αη=1 are explicitly retained.",
        "Pointwise conjugation C is real linear; it is distinct from operator adjoint. Complex-root preservation and descent remain separate obligations."
      ],
      "formulae": [
        {
          "label": "Actual PBPS squared defect: positive complex lift",
          "tex": "D=I-T^2\\ge0\\text{ on actual }L^2(\\nu;\\mathbb R),\\quad D_{\\mathbb C}g=\\iota D(\\operatorname{Re}g)+i\\iota D(\\operatorname{Im}g),\\quad D_{\\mathbb C}\\ge0,\\quad D_{\\mathbb C}\\iota=\\iota D,\\quad CD_{\\mathbb C}=D_{\\mathbb C}C."
        }
      ],
